;; it-prio-jump.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-prio-jump.s` (P2-SCALAR.4).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py it-prio-jump.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "it-prio-jump.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-prio-jump.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05), against the reference behaviors MEASURED by probe `prio-jump` (sail-riscv 0.14 AND" "spike 1.1.1-dev) before this guest existed — the leaf design records the measurements. The trap" "step is last: a contained trap stops the laboratory run. ⭐ x5 must NEVER be written: an" "instruction that raises a synchronous exception retires no architectural write (the DEFECT-B pin).")
(expectations (program "it-prio-jump.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 3) (never_written "x5") (step (n 0) (insn "lui x1, 0x40000") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "0x40000 << 12 = 0x40000000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing. The address is outside sail-riscv's MainMemory region, outside spike's DRAM, and no device on either platform — the unmapped half of the double fault.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "addi x1, x1, 3") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000040000003"))) (derivation "0x40000000 + 3 = 0x40000003. Odd, so JALR's low-bit clear (D-JALR-LSB) yields the target 0x40000002 — 2 mod 4, misaligned under IALIGN=32 — the misaligned half of the double fault.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-ALU-IMM)")) (step (n 2) (insn "jalr x5, x1, 0") (writes) (derivation "The target 0x40000002 is BOTH misaligned AND unmapped. The misalignment is judged on the jump, before any fetch is attempted at the target, so instruction-address-misaligned wins: cause 0x00, tval = the target value — measured identical on both references (probe prio-jump) — and the link write to x5 is SUPPRESSED (the DEFECT-B rule: a trapping instruction retires no write).") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.1 (D-JALR-LSB); §1.1.5.2 (D-MISALIGN-REPORT: raised on the jump, tval = the target)")))
